# t14_batch_cap.ledc -- THE 50-ENTRIES-PER-TIMESTAMP CAP.  ~13 s
# NOT therapeutic.  Feature family: executor limits.
# LINT: this file trips LEDC_BATCH_CAP (error) ON PURPOSE -- the cap IS the
# thing under test.  It also trips LEDC_MASK_HIGH_BITS (info) for the tick
# primer, like every other file here.
#
# config_parser.c:698-709 / 1942-1952: only the first 50 entries sharing a
# timestamp ever execute.  The "find the next strictly later timestamp" scan
# walks straight past the leftovers, so they NEVER FIRE -- silently, with no log
# line at all.  That makes it a direct cause of "events that seem not to fire",
# and it is the one device limit with NO runtime diagnostic, which is why a
# reproducer is worth having.
#
# CONSTRUCTION.  54 entries share t=1000, in file order:
#   entry   1       mask 16 @ 40 Hz, bright 0   -> the tick primer, executes
#   entries 2..50   mask 3  @ 10 Hz             -> all execute (identical, so
#                                                  the 50th simply re-anchors
#                                                  the same state)
#   entries 51..54  mask 12 @  7 Hz             -> DROPPED
# So the grade is a single unambiguous optical fact: lane A's eye (capture ch4)
# flickers at 10 Hz and lane B's eye (capture ch3) stays DARK, with no 7 Hz line
# anywhere.  If mask 12 flickers, the cap has moved and every "why did my event
# not fire" diagnosis built on it needs revisiting.
#
# The over-capped timestamp is deliberately NOT the last one in the file.  When
# the FINAL timestamp overflows, the leftovers keep the executor's "more entries
# to schedule" branch alive and the end-of-timeline stop_flicker_masked(0xFF) is
# never reached -- the LEDs are then left flickering for ever.  That is a real
# failure mode but an unsafe thing to ship as a test session, so it is listed in
# the README as deliberately not covered.
#
#
#
# CAPTURE-INTEGRITY CARRIER (audio ch15, 1900 Hz sine, hard LEFT, vol 40, from
# t=700 ms to the end of the file).  This is measurement scaffolding, not
# content.  A recorder can lose a block of frames mid-capture and still write a
# file of exactly the right length -- the missing TIME is simply absent -- and
# the frame-count check is blind to it.  Five such steps were found in one 665 s
# capture (~1 per 2.2 min), and one of them was written up as a firmware defect
# because BOTH optical sensors agreed on it: the whole recording had stepped.
#   python3 tools/avmeasure/captureintegrity.py rec.wav --carrier 1900 --audio-ch 1
# The tool needs a CONTINUOUS SINE: a session cycling square/saw/noise carriers
# gives ~369 us of phase noise against ~1 us for a sine, which inflates its
# self-calibrating threshold into a rubber stamp.  Hard LEFT so the RIGHT capture
# channel stays free of it for envelope and avsync work.  The marker window
# (0..600 ms) is not covered by this carrier; check it separately with
# --carrier 3000.
# CAPTURE-CHANNEL MAP used throughout sessions/test (see README.md):
#   capture ch1,ch2 = device headphone jack L,R   capture ch3 = photocell on
#   lane B's eye (LED3+LED4, mask 12)             capture ch4 = photocell on
#   lane A's eye (LED1+LED2, mask 3).
# --------------------------------------------------------------- sync marker
0     40 50 100 255 255 255 15
A 0   3000 0 70 0 1
600   0 50 0 0 0 0 15
A 600 0 0 0 0 1

# ---- capture-integrity carrier: continuous 1900 Hz sine, ch15, hard LEFT
A 700 1900 -100 40 0 15 0 0

# ---- B1  1..13 s : 54 entries at one timestamp (50 execute, 4 are dropped).
#      Entry 1 is the usual ISR tick primer (see any other file in this
#      directory for why it is needed); it also occupies the first of the 50
#      execution slots, which is why only 49 mask-3 rows follow.
1000 40 50 0 0 0 0 16 0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0    # execution slot 02 of 50
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0    # execution slot 50 of 50

# entries 51..54: past the cap, so these NEVER run and mask 12 stays dark
1000  7 50 100 255 255 255 12 0 0    # entry 51 -- DROPPED
1000  7 50 100 255 255 255 12 0 0    # entry 52 -- DROPPED
1000  7 50 100 255 255 255 12 0 0    # entry 53 -- DROPPED
1000  7 50 100 255 255 255 12 0 0    # entry 54 -- DROPPED
# ---- end
13000 0 50 0 0 0 0 15
13000 0 50 0 0 0 0 16                     # stop the tick primer too
A 13000 1900 -100 0 0 15 0 0            # stop the integrity carrier
